    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_62901442",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two images: the top image shows a group of people holding a framed photo of a person with pink hair and makeup, with the text 'no to transphobes,' while the bottom image shows a person in a Pride flag, with the text 'give trans people peace.' The overall intent is to portray transphobia as a problem that needs to be addressed, but the framing of the top image, with the group holding a framed photo of a person who appears to be a trans woman, may be interpreted as mocking or ridiculing trans people. The meme uses the visual of the framed photo to suggest that trans people are being 'boxed in' or 'contained,' which can be seen as a harmful and hateful representation. The meme's intent is to provoke a reaction and to suggest that transphobia is a problem that needs to be addressed, but the way it is presented may be seen as offensive and harmful to the trans community.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f873fd66"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
