      "label": "mocking and condescending emotion",
      "description": "The top image portrays a group of people holding a framed photo of a trans woman, with the text 'no to transphobes'. The framing of the photo, combined with the group's playful posing, suggests a mocking or condescending attitude toward trans people, implying they are 'boxed in' or 'contained'. This visual metaphor is used to express disdain or ridicule, which is a form of transphobic stereotype.",
